			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Drop redundant Effect.runPromise wrapper from Wind bootstrap\n\nThe `runBootstrap` export from `@codeeditorland/wind/Target/Effect/Bootstrap` already returns a Promise, making the `Effect.runPromise()` wrapper and the corresponding `Effect` import a redundant indirection layer.\n\nRemove the unused `Effect` import from both `Electron/Bootstrap.ts` and `Mountain.astro`, and replace the `Effect.runPromise(runBootstrap(...))` call in Mountain.astro with a plain `await runBootstrap(...)`. Also add an inline comment in `InstallProgressTerminalWorkspace.ts` documenting how cancellable progress routes through `IProgressService.withProgress` on the workbench side.\n\nThe bootstrap path is now one async indirection leaner with one fewer runtime dependency import.",
			"SHA": "4a3290c96ab9823bbbff63d3051d4e62c5f6b0b7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:24:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Route cancellable progress Cancel button to extension host via Cocoon\n\nWire cancellable progress notifications through `IProgressService.withProgress` directly so its `onDidCancel` third argument forwards the Cancel button click to the extension host as a `cancellable:notify('progress.cancel', { handle })` invocation.\n\nAdd a `CancellableProgress` map (`Map<string, {Resolve, Report}>`) with `StartCancellableProgress`, `EndCancellableProgress`, and `NotifyProgressCancel` helpers. The start handler checks `cancellable === true` and, when the workbench service is available, routes through `withProgress` with a placeholder entry so mid-flight updates before the task callback runs still resolve correctly. The update, complete, and end handlers check the map first before falling through to the existing `ShowProgress`/`UpdateProgress`/`DismissProgress` helpers.\n\nThe existing `ShowProgress(id, title, cancellable)` helper receives the cancellable flag through its `IProgressOptions` parameter but does not surface the `onDidCancel` hook, leaving the notification Cancel button non-functional for progress started via SkyBridge. Routing cancellable entries through `withProgress` directly gives the extension host full visibility into user cancellation intent.",
			"SHA": "0213fa8555c57ef9d1eeeba030bb70389e1b3e17"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:06:12Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				154,
				2
			],
			"Message": "perf(Sky): Parallelize extension scanning, inject modulepreload hints, enable terser minification\n\nOptimise the Astro build pipeline for both developer iteration speed and production load performance.\n\n**BakeExtensionManifest — dev-rebuild debounce and parallel root scanning:**\nAdd a module-level `LastScanAt` timestamp guard so hot-reload rebuilds that fire the `astro:build:done` hook more than once within 5 s skip re-scanning the extension directories entirely, cutting repeated I/O during fast edit-save cycles. Replace the sequential `for` loop over extension roots with `Promise.all(…map(ScanRoot))` so the two extension directories are scanned concurrently, reducing single-build wall-clock time.\n\n**InjectModulePreload — new Astro build integration:**\nRegister an `astro:build:done` hook (before CompressBundle, so injected links survive compression) that parses each workbench page's `<script type=\"module\">` entry chunks, walks their `__vite__mapDeps` reference arrays plus static and (for entry chunks) dynamic import paths, and emits one `<link rel=\"modulepreload\">` hint per transitive static dep, up to 40 links per page. Without this, the WKWebView discovers the boot chain (Preload → Polyfills → Bootstrap → Workbench → SkyBridge plus their static deps) one module-graph level at a time; the hints let the browser preload the full dependency tree before execution reaches each `import()` call.\n\n**Rollup terser minification:**\nEnable `minify: 'terser'` for production builds when the VS Code workbench is not bundled into the Rollup graph (i.e. `BundledActive` is false). In bundled mode the ~44 MB `vs/**` workbench chunk would add prohibitive time and `drop_console` would strip VS Code's own diagnostics, so minification is skipped. Clarify the sourcemap comment to document why `true` is used instead of `'hidden'`: WKWebView DevTools needs the `//# sourceMappingURL=` trailing comment to discover sibling `.map` files through the `land://` static server.",
			"SHA": "64cdae903ed7825691e14f5e33543f285b44be09"
		}
